    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but some of those arguments feel a bit superficial. Like, when people complain about 'neighborhood character,' is there actually a substantive economic or social argument there, or is it mostly just people being resistant to change? I want to make sure I'm not wasting time on arguments that don't hold water.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
