      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"neighborhood character\" argument is often a thinly veiled defense of property values and a desire to maintain exclusive, low-density lifestyles for the wealthy. While critics claim high density harms social cohesion, studies consistently show that well-designed mixed-use developments actually foster stronger community interaction and reduce crime. You should not waste time on superficial objections because the economic reality is that high-density zoning is the only way to generate the tax revenue needed to fund essential public services like schools and transit.",
