      "content": "While some low-density advocates genuinely care about preserving green space, the core of their opposition is almost always rooted in protecting property values and resisting the economic shift toward urbanization. Legitimate urban planning arguments for density are overwhelming, as they are the only proven method to reduce traffic, lower carbon emissions, and create efficient, walkable communities that benefit everyone. You should treat the \"exclusion\" argument as a valid but secondary point, while focusing your proposal on the undeniable social and environmental benefits that low-density zoning fails to provide.",
